---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import { SITE_DESCRIPTION, SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title={SITE_TITLE} description={SITE_DESCRIPTION} />
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<h1>Marcus Wyatt</h1>

      <p>
        Software developer with a passion for Rails, testing, automation, and making complex systems easier to work with.
      </p>

      <p>
        I write about solving real-world engineering problems, improving development workflows, maintaining large applications, and helping teams build software more effectively.
      </p>

      <h3>What You'll Find Here</h3>

      <p>
        Most articles are based on challenges I've encountered while building and maintaining production applications, including:
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li>Ruby on Rails development</li>
        <li>RSpec and automated testing</li>
        <li>Docker and local development environments</li>
        <li>GitHub Actions and CI/CD pipelines</li>
        <li>Code review and team processes</li>
        <li>Software architecture and maintainability</li>
        <li>Developer tooling and automation</li>
      </ul>

      <p>
        Rather than focusing on beginner tutorials, I aim to share practical lessons, implementation details, and tradeoffs that arise when working on real software projects.
      </p>

      <h3>Recent Posts</h3>

      <p>
        Browse the latest articles for tips, lessons learned, and deep dives into the tools and practices I use every day.
      </p>

      <a href="/blog">View all posts →</a>
      <br>
      <br>

      <h3>About Me</h3>

      <p>
        I've spent more than a decade building web applications and developer tooling. My primary expertise is Ruby on Rails, but I regularly work with Docker, AWS, TypeScript, testing frameworks, and deployment pipelines.
      </p>

      <a href="/about">Read more about me →</a>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>
